        "original_id": "f5fe6b23-52b4-50e5-9f73-0d8bb4e2f00e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Lomonosov\n- Products: Akademik Lomonosov\n- Organizations: Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant\n- Concepts: scientific discoveries, Law of Mass Conservation, atmosphere of Venus\n\nFacts:\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov lived from November 19, 1711, to April 15, 1765, and he was a Russian polymath, scientist, and writer.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov made important contributions to literature, education, and science.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov discovered the atmosphere of Venus and the Law of Mass Conservation in chemical reactions.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov worked across natural science, chemistry, physics, mineralogy, history, art, philology, and optical devices.\n- The ship Akademik Lomonosov was named after Academician Mikhail Lomonosov.\n- Plans were announced to begin shutting down Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant in 2019.\n- Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant was to be replaced by the floating nuclear power station Akademik Lomonosov.",
